    "body": "## What\nWhen the configured fused DSA backend declines a hook (`run_fused_qk_topk`, `run_fused_qk_topk_with_loss`, `run_fused_absorbed_sparse_attention`, `run_fused_dsa_attention`), the caller falls back to the PyTorch reference path. That path is far slower and materializes much larger tensors; the naive top-k builds the full `[sq, b, h, sk]` fp32 score tensor.\n\n`_log_declined_hook` logged this at DEBUG on every call, so a run could sit on the reference path with nothing in the logs. This changes it to a WARNING emitted once per (backend, hook, reason).\n\n## Why once\nDeclines happen on every forward, so a per-call warning would flood the logs. The key keeps distinct reasons visible.\n\n## Testing\n- **Unit test:** `test_dsa_kernel_hooks_log_declined_backend` now asserts the message is visible at WARNING level and that a repeat decline doesn't log again. It and `test_dsa_kernel_hooks_dispatch_to_backend` pass on this branch (GB300).\n- **Downstream check:** on a downstream fork, a healthy GLM-family DSA run (cuDNN backend, 262k and packed 8x32k) emits no declined warnings, so this doesn't add noise to normal runs.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
